language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place coins on an n by n grid so that every row and every column holds exactly c coins, at most one coin per cell, minimising the sum of the squared horizontal distances of the coins from the main diagonal.
given n : int(1..)
given c : int(1..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of bool
find rowcost : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..c*n*n)
find z : int(0..c*n*n*n)

branching on [x]
heuristic sdf

minimising z

such that
$ the squared horizontal distance of the coins in row i from the main diagonal is rowcost[i]
forAll i : int(1..n) . rowcost[i] = sum j : int(1..n) . (i - j) * (i - j) * toInt(x[i,j]),
$ the sum of the quadratic horizontal distance from the main diagonal of all cells containing a coin is z
z = sum i : int(1..n) . rowcost[i],
$ a row with i in it holds c coins, which are at least as far from the diagonal as the c nearest columns, so rowcost[i] is at least the cheapest window of c columns
forAll i : int(1..n) . rowcost[i] >= min([ sum j : int(s..s+c-1) . (i - j) * (i - j) | s : int(1..n-c+1) ]),
$ in each row exactly c coins must be placed
forAll i : int(1..n) . (sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(x[i,j])) = c,
$ in each column exactly c coins must be placed
forAll j : int(1..n) . (sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(x[i,j])) = c
